arguments.cmd:
cat > /app/output/poster.html <<'HTML'
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Bot Mitigation at Scale - Poster</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg0: #070B14;
      --bg1: #0B1220;
      --card: rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
      --card2: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
      --line: rgba(255,255,255,0.10);
      --text: rgba(255,255,255,0.92);
      --muted: rgba(255,255,255,0.70);
      --muted2: rgba(255,255,255,0.55);
      --accent: #00C2FF;
      --accent2: #23F0C7;
      --warn: #FFB020;
      --good: #3DFF7A;
      --mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", "Courier New", monospace;
      --sans: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, "Apple Color Emoji", "Segoe UI Emoji";
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }

    html, body {
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      background: radial-gradient(1100px 1100px at 20% 0%, rgba(0,194,255,0.10), transparent 50%),
                  radial-gradient(900px 900px at 95% 8%, rgba(35,240,199,0.10), transparent 55%),
                  linear-gradient(180deg, var(--bg0), var(--bg1) 55%, #050712);
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: var(--sans);
    }

    /* A1 portrait @ 150 DPI approximation: 7016×9933 */
    .poster {
      width: 7016px;
      height: 9933px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 220px 220px 210px;
      position: relative;
    }

    .topbar {
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 48px;
      padding-bottom: 56px;
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line);
    }

    .title {
      max-width: 80%;
    }

    .title h1 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 138px;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      line-height: 1.06;
      font-weight: 850;
    }

    .title p {
      margin: 26px 0 0;
      font-size: 56px;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.25;
    }

    .venue {
      text-align: right;
      padding-left: 30px;
    }

    .venue .tag {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 16px;
      padding: 16px 22px;
      border: 2px solid rgba(0,194,255,0.35);
      background: rgba(0,194,255,0.08);
      border-radius: 999px;
      font-size: 42px;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.92);
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .venue .tag .dot {
      width: 14px;
      height: 14px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--accent);
      box-shadow: 0 0 22px rgba(0,194,255,0.75);
    }

    .venue .meta {
      margin-top: 18px;
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 34px;
      color: var(--muted2);
    }

    .grid {
      margin-top: 72px;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr;
      gap: 60px;
    }

    .card {
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.07), rgba(255,255,255,0.03));
      border: 2px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 34px;
      padding: 54px;
      box-shadow: 0 30px 70px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .card::before {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      inset: -2px;
      background: radial-gradient(600px 260px at 10% 0%, rgba(0,194,255,0.12), transparent 60%),
                  radial-gradient(520px 240px at 95% 10%, rgba(35,240,199,0.10), transparent 60%);
      pointer-events: none;
      z-index: 0;
    }

    .card > * { position: relative; z-index: 1; }

    .card h2 {
      margin: 0 0 22px;
      font-size: 66px;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }

    .card p {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 44px;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.38;
    }

    .metrics {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 34px;
      margin-top: 30px;
    }

    .metric {
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
      border: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.10);
      border-radius: 28px;
      padding: 34px 34px 30px;
      min-height: 240px;
    }

    .metric .value {
      font-size: 110px;
      font-weight: 900;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      line-height: 1.0;
      color: var(--accent);
      text-shadow: 0 0 46px rgba(0,194,255,0.25);
    }

    .metric.big {
      grid-column: span 2;
      min-height: 290px;
      border-color: rgba(0,194,255,0.35);
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(0,194,255,0.14), rgba(0,194,255,0.04));
    }

    .metric.big .value {
      font-size: 170px;
    }

    .metric.good {
      border-color: rgba(61,255,122,0.30);
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(61,255,122,0.10), rgba(255,255,255,0.03));
    }

    .metric.good .value {
      color: var(--good);
      text-shadow: 0 0 46px rgba(61,255,122,0.20);
    }

    .metric .label {
      margin-top: 14px;
      font-size: 40px;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.78);
      line-height: 1.25;
    }

    .metric .note {
      margin-top: 10px;
      font-size: 34px;
      color: var(--muted2);
      line-height: 1.25;
      font-family: var(--mono);
    }

    .subgrid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 60px;
    }

    .pipeline {
      margin-top: 26px;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 24px;
    }

    .step {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 92px 1fr 230px;
      gap: 24px;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 28px 28px;
      border-radius: 24px;
      border: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.10);
      background: rgba(0,0,0,0.18);
    }

    .step .idx {
      width: 92px;
      height: 92px;
      border-radius: 22px;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      font-weight: 900;
      font-size: 44px;
      background: rgba(0,194,255,0.12);
      border: 2px solid rgba(0,194,255,0.30);
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.92);
      box-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(0,194,255,0.16);
    }

    .step .main {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 8px;
    }

    .step .main .name {
      font-size: 46px;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }

    .step .main .desc {
      font-size: 38px;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.25;
    }

    .step .dur {
      justify-self: end;
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 36px;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.78);
      padding: 14px 18px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12);
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .arrow {
      height: 34px;
      margin: 0 14px;
      position: relative;
    }

    .arrow::before {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      left: 60px;
      right: 60px;
      top: 16px;
      height: 2px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(0,194,255,0.60), transparent);
    }

    .arrow::after {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      left: calc(50% - 10px);
      top: 5px;
      width: 20px;
      height: 20px;
      border-right: 3px solid rgba(0,194,255,0.60);
      border-bottom: 3px solid rgba(0,194,255,0.60);
      transform: rotate(45deg);
    }

    .table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: separate;
      border-spacing: 0;
      margin-top: 26px;
      overflow: hidden;
      border-radius: 26px;
      border: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.10);
      background: rgba(0,0,0,0.20);
    }

    .table th, .table td {
      padding: 24px 24px;
      font-size: 38px;
      text-align: left;
    }

    .table th {
      font-size: 36px;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85);
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
      border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.10);
      font-weight: 800;
    }

    .table td {
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.78);
      border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
    }

    .table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }

    .table .emph {
      font-weight: 900;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.92);
    }

    .table .after {
      color: rgba(61,255,122,0.90);
      font-weight: 850;
    }

    .table .before {
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.72);
    }

    .tradeoffs {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 26px;
      margin-top: 26px;
    }

    .pill {
      padding: 26px 26px 24px;
      border-radius: 26px;
      border: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.10);
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
      min-height: 210px;
    }

    .pill .head {
      display: flex;
      gap: 16px;
      align-items: center;
      font-size: 44px;
      font-weight: 850;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }

    .pill .icon {
      width: 46px;
      height: 46px;
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: rgba(35,240,199,0.12);
      border: 2px solid rgba(35,240,199,0.30);
      box-shadow: 0 0 24px rgba(35,240,199,0.16);
    }

    .pill p {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 38px;
      line-height: 1.32;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .footer {
      position: absolute;
      left: 220px;
      right: 220px;
      bottom: 130px;
      padding-top: 36px;
      border-top: 2px solid var(--line);
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 40px;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }

    .footer .k {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 30px;
      color: var(--muted2);
      line-height: 1.35;
    }

    .footer .k strong {
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.88);
      font-weight: 800;
    }

    .badge {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 14px;
      padding: 10px 16px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.10);
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 28px;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.75);
    }

    .badge .ray {
      color: rgba(0,194,255,0.95);
    }

    .mini {
      font-size: 30px;
      color: var(--muted2);
    }

    .tight { margin-top: 18px; }

  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="poster">
    <div class="topbar">
      <div class="title">
        <h1>Bot Mitigation at Scale</h1>
        <p>How modern CDN-based web security services protect scientific publishing platforms from automated threats.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="venue">
        <div class="tag"><span class="dot"></span> IEEE Symposium on Security and Privacy (S&amp;P)</div>
        <div class="meta">Case: www.science.org · DOI: 10.1126/science.add1585</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid">
      <!-- Left column: metrics + outcomes + tradeoffs -->
      <div class="subgrid">
        <div class="card">
          <h2>The Bot Threat Landscape for Academic Publishers</h2>
          <p>High-value full-text articles, supplementary datasets, and identifiers (e.g., DOIs) make publisher platforms prime targets for large-scale scraping, credential stuffing, and surge traffic.</p>

          <div class="metrics">
            <div class="metric big">
              <div class="value">85%</div>
              <div class="label">Reduction in unauthorized bulk scraping attempts (first 6 months)</div>
              <div class="note">~1.2M/day → ~180k/day</div>
            </div>

            <div class="metric good">
              <div class="value">99.97%</div>
              <div class="label">Uptime maintained during bot surges</div>
              <div class="note">Surges &gt;10× baseline traffic</div>
            </div>

            <div class="metric">
              <div class="value">~47%</div>
              <div class="label">Estimated share of 2024 internet traffic from bots</div>
              <div class="note">~30% malicious bot share (of bots)</div>
            </div>

            <div class="metric">
              <div class="value">&lt;2s</div>
              <div class="label">Typical end-to-end verification latency for legitimate users</div>
              <div class="note">Added page-load overhead &lt;150ms (verified sessions)</div>
            </div>

            <div class="metric">
              <div class="value">&lt;0.3%</div>
              <div class="label">Legitimate users reporting access friction</div>
              <div class="note">Measured via user complaints</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="tight mini">Key takeaway: challenge-based verification at the CDN edge sharply reduces scraping while keeping availability near-perfect.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h2>Performance and Security Outcomes</h2>
          <p>Measured changes before vs. after CDN-level bot mitigation deployment on a major science publisher platform.</p>

          <table class="table" aria-label="before after outcomes">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Metric</th>
                <th>Before</th>
                <th>After</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td class="emph">Scraping attempts per day</td>
                <td class="before">~1.2 million</td>
                <td class="after">~180,000</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="emph">Avg. origin server load (CPU %)</td>
                <td class="before">78%</td>
                <td class="after">42%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="emph">Legitimate user complaints (monthly)</td>
                <td class="before">1,200</td>
                <td class="after">340</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="emph">Uptime during bot surges</td>
                <td class="before">98.5%</td>
                <td class="after">99.97%</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <div class="tight">
            <span class="badge">Traceability: <span class="ray">Ray ID</span> enables request-level investigation</span>
            <span class="badge">Added edge latency: &lt;150ms (verified)</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h2>Usability vs. Security Trade-offs</h2>
          <p>Blocking automation is only half the problem—publisher platforms must preserve legitimate researcher access.</p>
          <div class="tradeoffs">
            <div class="pill">
              <div class="head"><span class="icon"></span>Accessibility (WCAG 2.1)</div>
              <p>Challenge pages must be usable by people with disabilities; poor implementations can exclude legitimate users.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pill">
              <div class="head"><span class="icon"></span>Institutional Access</div>
              <p>Allowlisting university IP ranges reduces unnecessary challenges for campus networks while preserving security controls elsewhere.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pill">
              <div class="head"><span class="icon"></span>Transparency</div>
              <p>Clear messaging (e.g., “Performing security verification…”) improves user trust during brief delays.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pill">
              <div class="head"><span class="icon"></span>Privacy</div>
              <p>Threat detection uses fingerprinting and behavioral signals; platforms must disclose data practices and minimize collection.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right column: verification pipeline -->
      <div class="subgrid">
        <div class="card">
          <h2>Challenge-Based Verification Pipeline</h2>
          <p>CDN-edge interception evaluates risk signals and issues challenges only when thresholds are exceeded.</p>

          <div class="pipeline" role="list">
            <div class="step" role="listitem">
              <div class="idx">1</div>
              <div class="main">
                <div class="name">Request Interception</div>
                <div class="desc">Incoming HTTP request routed via CDN edge node.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="dur">&lt; 50 ms</div>
            </div>
            <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>

            <div class="step" role="listitem">
              <div class="idx">2</div>
              <div class="main">
                <div class="name">Threat Scoring</div>
                <div class="desc">IP reputation, TLS fingerprint, and behavioral signals evaluated.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="dur">~ 100 ms</div>
            </div>
            <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>

            <div class="step" role="listitem">
              <div class="idx">3</div>
              <div class="main">
                <div class="name">Challenge Issuance</div>
                <div class="desc">JavaScript or CAPTCHA served when risk score exceeds threshold.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="dur">~ 500 ms</div>
            </div>
            <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>

            <div class="step" role="listitem">
              <div class="idx">4</div>
              <div class="main">
                <div class="name">Verification Check</div>
                <div class="desc">Client response validated; trace identifier assigned (Ray ID).</div>
              </div>
              <div class="dur">~ 200 ms</div>
            </div>
            <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>

            <div class="step" role="listitem">
              <div class="idx">5</div>
              <div class="main">
                <div class="name">Access Grant</div>
                <div class="desc">Verified request forwarded to origin with session token.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="dur">&lt; 50 ms</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="tight mini">Automation lacking JS execution is blocked; legitimate users typically complete the pipeline in under 2 seconds.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
          <div class="tradeoffs" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr;">
            <div class="pill" style="min-height: unset;">
              <div class="head"><span class="icon"></span>Scale</div>
              <p>Bots account for a large fraction of internet traffic, and publisher sites see disproportionate scraping pressure.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pill" style="min-height: unset;">
              <div class="head"><span class="icon"></span>Mechanism</div>
              <p>Multi-stage, CDN-edge verification blocks most malicious automation while allowing humans through with minimal overhead.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pill" style="min-height: unset;">
              <div class="head"><span class="icon"></span>Measurement</div>
              <p>Request-level tracing (e.g., Ray IDs) supports tuning thresholds to minimize friction and maximize bot blocking.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pill" style="min-height: unset;">
              <div class="head"><span class="icon"></span>Collaboration</div>
              <p>Publishers and CDN providers must co-design policies to keep scientific knowledge accessible and resilient.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="footer">
      <div class="k"><strong>Scope:</strong> CDN-level bot mitigation (e.g., Cloudflare) for scientific publishing platforms.<br/>
      <strong>Audience:</strong> Security researchers &amp; practitioners · data-forward, operationally grounded.<br/>
      <span class="mini">This poster synthesizes a case study narrative and aggregated metrics; values shown are as reported in the provided brief.</span></div>
      <div class="k" style="text-align:right;">
        <strong>Artifacts:</strong> HTTP interception → scoring → challenge → verification → access grant<br/>
        <strong>Identifiers:</strong> DOI, Ray ID (trace), session token (access)
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
